 ### [Vector Icon Volume Rendering](7693-vector-icon-volume-rendering.md)
-Vector Icon Volume Rendering is a 3D raster resampling technique that integrates flow direction and magnitude into volume rendering by embedding small billboard images containing vector icons within splat footprints. It solves the problem of visualizing vector fields (such as wind velocity) within scalar volumes (such as density clouds) by creating an illusion of coherent flow through stochastic placement and compositing of these icons. Unlike standard direct volume ray casting which relies on scalar opacity and color, this method modifies the volume integral to include the rendering of tiny cylinders or icons, oriented parallel to the projected vector direction. It sets itself apart from sibling methods like [Texture-Based Volume Rendering](4707-texture-based-volume-rendering.md) by using discrete, billboard-oriented icons rather than continuous anisotropic textures, and from [View-Aligned Slicing](6530-view-aligned-slicing.md) by explicitly embedding vector geometry into the splat footprint rather than just slicing the volume.
